  "scoring_methodology": "baseline_severity: max of three per-meter-normalized signal strengths (deviation_z, pct_change_prev, same-week deviation / rolling_std_1d), each clipped via its own review/high threshold. isolation_forest_severity: percentile rank of the raw anomaly score against that meter's OWN TRAINING-SET score distribution (not the scoring window) - fixed in Phase B.1 from an earlier per-window min-max scaling that forced every scoring window to span 0-100 regardless of actual anomalousness. combined_severity: max(baseline_strength, isolation_forest_strength), where each component is converted to a 0-1 strength using ITS OWN thresholds before combining (isolation_forest_review_percentile=90/isolation_forest_high_percentile=97 for IF, since its percentile scale is not comparable to baseline's 0-100 scale) - this combination-level fix was also added in Phase B.1 after the naive shared-threshold combination produced an 83% flag rate from Isolation Forest alone on real data.",
